  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between (-)-Menthyl propionate and ZR-75-1 through a series of molecular targets. The drug (-)-Menthyl propionate is identified as a target of SNU-387, which in turn is a target of multiple compounds, including (1S,3R,6S,8R,12S,15R,16R)-15-[(2R)-4-[(2R)-3,3-dimethyloxiran-2-yl]butan-2-yl]-7,7,12,16-tetramethylpentacyclo[9.7.0.01,3.03,8.012,16]octadecan-6-ol and 5-Hydroxytryptophan monohydrate, dl-. All of these compounds are ultimately linked to ZR-75-1, indicating a possible pathway where (-)-Menthyl propionate may influence ZR-75-1 through these intermediates. The evidence suggests that the drug may act as a modulator or inhibitor of a pathway involving SNU-387, which in turn interacts with ZR-75-1. The integration of these targets highlights a potential mechanism where (-)-Menthyl propionate could exert its effects via a series of molecular interactions that ultimately lead to the interaction with ZR-75-1.",
